                <pb facs="0590" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1189: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jordan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-16T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Your despatch 564, January 4, 1921 [<hi rendition="#italic">1922</hi>].</p>
                <p>Inform Haitian Government in reply to its memorandum to you, dated December 30th,
                    that Department cannot take into consideration any suggestion questioning
                    validity of the Protocol, which this Government considers to be in full force
                    and effect, and must stand upon its suggestion that authorization be sent to the
                    Financial Adviser to undertake formal negotiations for a loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
